# Engine-contract golden produced by the reference probe: generated by run.sh, do not edit.
# The see-creature tick scan and the tick on which a first attack desire turns into the attack intention.
# Format: internal/gameserver/script/testdata/oracle/README.md, "Contract golden format".

table aggro.first_tick
source java/net/sf/l2j/gameserver/model/actor/ai/type/NpcAI.java 449-575 runAI
source java/net/sf/l2j/gameserver/model/actor/ai/type/NpcAI.java 698-726 addAttackDesire
provenance probe java=55ff8a4ec7e186d9816cd549246b4cf1f59c9f12 datapack=55ff8a4ec7e186d9816cd549246b4cf1f59c9f12
note An NPC (20049, its scripts replaced by one see-creature script) is taken off the AI task manager; each tick is one runAI() call (the task manager's 1 s call). The script, where attack is on, adds an attack desire of 200 on the seen creature, as the aggressive behaviors' tryToAttack does. Lines: per tick, the see-creature calls inside it, then the intention and lifetime after it.
note addAttackDesire runs a nested runAI(false) when the aggro list has no most-hated creature; runAI decides whether it may pick a desire (instantRun) before the see-creature scan, from the lifetime and the queued desires. Default see range 450; p is in range at 100, out of range at 1000.
row fresh-npc-sees-attacks attack=true start=in age=0 aggro_list_held=false
  setup lifetime=0 intention=IDLE p=in
  tick 1
    see p lifetime=0 intention=IDLE
    add attack desire on p -> intention=ATTACK
    after intention=ATTACK lifetime=1
  tick 2
    after intention=ATTACK lifetime=2
  tick 3
    after intention=ATTACK lifetime=3
row aged-npc-sees-attacks attack=true start=out age=3 aggro_list_held=false
  setup lifetime=3 intention=IDLE p=out
  p moves in range
  tick 1
    see p lifetime=3 intention=IDLE
    add attack desire on p -> intention=ATTACK
    after intention=ATTACK lifetime=4
  tick 2
    after intention=ATTACK lifetime=5
